# Fork-owned files for arrrrny/herdr.
#
# Each line is `<path>  ::  <marker>`. The sync-upstream workflow greps
# `<path>` for `<marker>` after every clean merge. If the marker is gone,
# upstream silently overwrote a fork-owned feature and the sync fails.
#
# Add an entry every time you change a fork-owned file. Pick a marker
# that is unique enough that a clean upstream edit cannot accidentally
# remove it. Issue references (e.g. `arrrrny/herdr#1`) work well because
# upstream does not know about the fork's issue tracker.

